47	- each reaction is its own listener, with its own rules about when to act;
48	- the reactions that existed before are listeners too, not direct calls next to the new ones;
49	- the list of listeners is assembled outside the source, where the application is wired;
50	- adding a reaction means one new listener and one line where they are registered.
51	
